1
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
A Flintstone Christmas is a animation, tv movie, comedy
film directed by Charles August Nichols.

2
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Santa has an accident at Fred's house on Christmas Eve, Fred
and Barney have to continue his run for him.

3
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Fred Flintstone (voice), played by Henry Corden.

4
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Barney Rubble / Dino (voice), played by Mel Blanc.

5
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Wilma Flintstone / Pebbles Flintstone (voice), played by Jean Vander Pyl.

6
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Betty Rubble (voice), played by Gay Autterson.

7
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Bamm Bamm Rubble (voice), played by Lucille Bliss.

8
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Mr. George Nate Slate (voice), played by John Stephenson.

9
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
A Flintstone Christmas is a 1977 animated Christmas television special
featuring characters from The Flintstones franchise.

10
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
It was produced by Hanna-Barbera and is the second Christmas-themed animated work in the franchise, after the 1964
episode "Christmas Flintstone." Both feature the character Fred Flintstone taking on the role of Santa Claus.

11
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
The special first aired on NBC on December 7, 1977.

12
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
The special has been released on VHS and DVD.

13
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
It is followed by two more Flintstones Christmas specials, A Flintstone
Family Christmas (1993) and A Flintstones Christmas Carol (1994).

14
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
The film explores themes of holiday, santa claus, family
relationships, alternate history, anachronism.

15
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
The tone is lighthearted.
